{
  // VoxEngine scenarios — a SEPARATE compilation from the Next app's.
  //
  // WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. `typings/voxengine.d.ts` is Voximplant's ambient
  // declaration file for their cloud runtime, and their own docs describe it as
  // an IDE aid: "for writing TypeScript code in your external IDE… add it to
  // your project folder, or specify it in the tsconfig.json". It used to be
  // picked up by the ROOT tsconfig's `**/*.ts` (a .d.ts is a TypeScript source
  // file for Program construction), which put 612 global `declare`s — `Call`,
  // `Player`, `WebSocket` among them — into the type program of every file in
  // the Next app. That is now excluded there, which left the declarations with
  // no config including them at all. This is that config.
  //
  // ⚠️ THIS IS NOT WHAT BUILDS THE SCENARIOS. `voxengine-ci` writes its own
  // `voxfiles/tsconfig.voxengine.temp.json` on every run, uses it, and deletes
  // it. This file is for the editor and for a manual `tsc -p voxfiles` check;
  // changing it cannot change what gets uploaded.
  //
  // SHAPE FOLLOWS THE VENDOR'S OWN EXAMPLE (docs.voximplant.ai/platform/
  // voxengine/ci.md), with two deliberate differences:
  //
  //   1. The path. Their example still says `voxfiles/scenarios/src` — the
  //      PRE-36 layout. 36.0.0 moved sources under `applications/<app>/`, and
  //      their docs have not caught up (the panel quickstart is stale the same
  //      way). Ours uses the real directory.
  //
  //   2. Both typing files, not one. Their example includes only the copy
  //      inside the package; `createOrUpdateTsConfig` includes THAT ONE AND
  //      `typings/` — so the build sees both, and so must this, or the editor
  //      would disagree with the build. The two versions differ (7.64.1 from
  //      the CDN vs 7.57.0 bundled) and conflict on hundreds of ambient
  //      identifiers, which is why `skipLibCheck` is on here exactly as it is
  //      in the generated config. MEASURED 2026-09-15: 0 errors with it, 67
  //      without. The ElevenLabs surface is identical across the two.
  //
  // `noEmit`: nothing here should produce files. Only voxengine-ci emits, into
  // its own dist/, and a stray build here would corrupt the upload hash.
  "compilerOptions": {
    "allowJs": true,
    "target": "ES2020",
    "lib": ["ES2020"],
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "noEmit": true,
    "checkJs": false
  },
  "include": [
    "applications/*/scenarios/src",
    "../typings/voxengine.d.ts",
    "../node_modules/@voximplant/voxengine-ci/typings"
  ],
  "exclude": ["../node_modules", "applications/*/scenarios/dist"]
}
